---
import NoteLayout from '../../layouts/NoteLayout.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'The Commodification of Content',
  description: 'When AI makes content infinitely cheap to produce, what happens to its value? An argument for why the lane is narrowing for generic content — and what survives.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Rankit Consultancy' },
  datePublished: '2026-04-04',
};
---
<NoteLayout
  title="The Commodification of Content"
  description="When AI makes content infinitely cheap to produce, what happens to its value? An argument for why the lane is narrowing for generic content — and what survives."
  articleSlug="the-commodification-of-content"
  schema={schema}
>
  <p class="description scribble-target">When the marginal cost of producing a piece of content approaches zero, its market value follows. This is not a prediction — it is already happening. The canvas is filling up.</p>

  <div class="filling-canvas-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
    <canvas id="filling-canvas" class="filling-canvas"></canvas>
  </div>

  <h2 class="note-heading">The Economics of Infinite Supply</h2>
  <p class="note-text">Content used to be constrained by time, expertise, and distribution. A well-researched article took hours. A good video took a crew. Those friction points were, paradoxically, the thing that gave content its value — scarcity created signal.</p>
  <p class="note-text">Generative AI removes that friction almost entirely. A thousand blog posts can be produced in the time it once took to write one. The supply curve shifts so far right that price collapses toward zero. This is commodification in its purest form.</p>

  <h2 class="note-heading">What Gets Squeezed First</h2>
  <ul class="note-list">
    <li>Thin informational content — "what is X", "how to do Y" — already being replaced by AI Overviews directly in search results.</li>
    <li>Listicles and aggregations with no original research or perspective.</li>
    <li>Content produced purely for ranking, with no genuine audience in mind.</li>
    <li>Anything a competent language model can reproduce without access to proprietary data or lived experience.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="note-heading">What Survives</h2>
  <p class="note-text">Commodification does not eliminate all value — it redistributes it. In every market that has undergone this shift, a new premium tier emerges alongside the commodity floor.</p>
  <ul class="note-list">
    <li><strong>Original research and proprietary data</strong> — things no model can fabricate without access to your sources.</li>
    <li><strong>Genuine expertise and opinion</strong> — a clearly held point of view from someone with skin in the game.</li>
    <li><strong>Community and trust</strong> — audiences that follow a person or brand, not just a topic.</li>
    <li><strong>Speed and context</strong> — real-time commentary on events as they unfold, before models are retrained.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="note-heading">The Strategic Implication</h2>
  <p class="note-text">If your content strategy is built on volume and coverage, you are competing in a space that fills up faster every quarter. The brands that will win are those that use AI to handle the commodity layer — freeing up human capacity for the work that cannot be replicated.</p>
  <p class="note-text">Every ball in the canvas is another piece of generic content. The blue one is yours.</p>
</NoteLayout>

<style>
  .filling-canvas-wrapper {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .filling-canvas {
    width: 100%;
    height: 120px;
    display: block;
  }
</style>

<script>
  function initFillingCanvas() {
    const canvas = document.getElementById('filling-canvas') as HTMLCanvasElement | null;
    if (!canvas) return;

    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    if (!ctx) return;

    let animId: number;
    let t = 0;

    const STAGGER = 10; // frames between each ball appearing
    const PAUSE = 100;  // frames to hold once canvas is full

    function frame() {
      const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
      const w = canvas!.clientWidth;
      const h = canvas!.clientHeight;
      canvas!.width = w * dpr;
      canvas!.height = h * dpr;
      ctx!.scale(dpr, dpr);

      const radius = h * 0.13;
      const spacing = radius * 2.6;
      const cols = Math.floor(w / spacing);
      const rows = Math.floor(h / spacing);
      const total = cols * rows;

      const offsetX = (w - cols * spacing) / 2 + radius;
      const offsetY = (h - rows * spacing) / 2 + radius;

      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);

      const toShow = Math.min(Math.floor(t / STAGGER), total);

      for (let i = 0; i < toShow; i++) {
        const col = i % cols;
        const row = Math.floor(i / cols);
        const x = offsetX + col * spacing;
        const y = offsetY + row * spacing;
        const isBlue = i === total - 1;

        ctx.globalAlpha = 0.9;
        ctx.fillStyle = isBlue ? '#3b82f6' : '#722f37';
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(x, y, radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();

        ctx.globalAlpha = 0.2;
        ctx.fillStyle = '#ffffff';
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(x - radius * 0.28, y - radius * 0.28, radius * 0.4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      }

      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      t++;
      if (t > total * STAGGER + PAUSE) t = 0;

      animId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    animId = requestAnimationFrame(frame);

    document.addEventListener('astro:before-preparation', () => {
      cancelAnimationFrame(animId);
    }, { once: true });
  }

  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initFillingCanvas);
</script>
